<script>
	import Callout from '$lib/components/Callout.svelte';
</script>

GraphQL shares ApiTool's request envelope — you just add `protocol: graphql` and a
`graphql:` block. Queries can live in their own `.graphql` files, fragments are
composed and topologically ordered for you, and because a GraphQL server can return
`200 OK` with an `errors` array, you choose explicitly how partial failures are
treated.

## The query and fragments

```graphql
# graphql/list-users.graphql
query ListUsers($limit: Int!) {
  users(first: $limit) {
    ...UserFields
    ...Timestamps
  }
}
```

```graphql
# graphql/fragments/user-fields.graphql
fragment UserFields on User {
  id
  name
  email
}
```

```graphql
# graphql/fragments/timestamps.graphql
fragment Timestamps on Node {
  createdAt
  updatedAt
}
```

## The collection

```yaml
# collections/graphql.yaml
name: GraphQL API
requests:
  - name: List users
    request:
      protocol: graphql
      url: "{{base_url}}/graphql"
      graphql:
        query_file: "graphql/list-users.graphql"
        fragments:
          - "graphql/fragments/user-fields.graphql"
          - "graphql/fragments/timestamps.graphql"
        variables:
          limit: 10
        error_handling: fail        # fail | warn | ignore
    assertions:
      status: 200
      body:
        "$.data.users":
          type: "array"
        "$.errors":
          not_exists: true
      cel:
        - "response.body.data.users.size() <= 10"
        - "response.body.data.users.all(u, u.email != '')"
```

The method is set to `POST` and `Content-Type: application/json` automatically; the
body becomes `{"query": "...", "variables": {...}}` with the fragments concatenated
ahead of the query.

## Choosing how errors are treated

A GraphQL response has four shapes, and `error_handling` decides each verdict:

| Outcome | `data` / `errors` | `fail` | `warn` | `ignore` |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| success | data, no errors | pass | pass | pass |
| partial | data **and** errors | fail | warn | pass |
| full failure | no data, errors | fail | warn | pass |
| empty | neither | pass | pass | pass |

## Run it

```bash
apitest run collections/graphql.yaml
```

```
Collection: GraphQL API
  ✓ List users  200  134ms

────────────────────────────────
  1 request(s): 1 passed, 0 failed (134ms)
```

